@startuml gui_class
title plogic - GUI

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class GUI {
  +{static} should_launch(argv: List<OsString>): bool
  +{static} run(): Result
}

class PlogicApp {
  -input: str
  -simplify: bool
  -show_table: bool
  -show_process: bool
  -outcome: Outcome?
  -cursor: CCursorRange?
  +evaluate()
  +insert_at_cursor(ctx: &Context, text: str)
}

class View {
  +assessments: List<Assessment>
  +show_table: bool
  +show_process: bool
}

enum Outcome {
  Evaluations(View)
  Errors(List<str>)
}

class Orchestrator

class Assessment {
  +formula: str
  +variables: int
  +simplification: Simplification?
  +table: TruthTable?
}

class TruthTable

class Simplification {
  +expression: Expression
  +steps: List<Step>
}

class Step {
  +rule: Rule
  +expression: Expression
}

note bottom of PlogicApp
  Fixed header and input section; only the result section
  scrolls. The result components are centered; the help is
  a collapsed single-column list at a smaller size. All
  three modes are snapshotted in View when Evaluar is
  pressed; changing one afterwards only affects the next
  evaluation. Mostrar tabla off calls assess with no table;
  on, assess builds only below ten variables. No table means
  no classification (ADR-049).
end note

GUI ..> PlogicApp : <<create>>
PlogicApp --> Outcome
Outcome --> View
View --> Assessment
PlogicApp ..> Orchestrator : assess(source, simplify, max_variables)
Assessment --> TruthTable
Assessment --> Simplification
Simplification --> Step : steps

@enduml
